        "process": "<ol><li><strong>Memory &amp; Scope Lock</strong>: The coordinator queries LanceDB for prior studio shader preferences, locks the target engine to native Godot 4.7 Forward+, and establishes a dual-deliverable plan (playable <code>.exe</code> vertical slice plus a <code>$19.99</code> marketplace kit).</li><li><strong>Wave-Based Parallel Production</strong>: Specialist subagents work in non-overlapping file shards—one builds headless Blender 5.1 Python scripts to kitbash and bake <code>2048x2048</code> Cycles PBR textures, another writes the stepped manga cel-shader and barcode-scanner physics, and a third builds live WebSocket redline and room-layout tools.</li><li><strong>Sequential 8 GB GPU Time-Slicing</strong>: To avoid out-of-memory crashes on our 8 GB RTX 4060 Laptop GPU, the pipeline unloads LM Studio weights, clears ComfyUI cache, runs headless Blender Cycles bakes, and then boots Godot Vulkan Movie Maker to record a deterministic 90-second (<code>2,160</code>-frame) walkthrough video.</li><li><strong>Adversarial Verification</strong>: Ten computer-vision audit lenses inspect every frame of the walkthrough video in SQLite while a separate Challenger agent runs <code>28</code> headless test suites.</li></ol>",
